--
-- Act I: Bookcase Interaction
--
SHARP_GUILT: Five days. You pulled these volumes down five days ago, swore you'd cross-reference the index, and let them pile like kindling. You can't even digest a paragraph that someone else already wrote for you.
FADING_LOGIC: Author, catalog, premise. It's an alphabetized storage system. Read the abstract. If you read just one summary, the bibliography shrinks.
PRIMARY_NARRATOR: Logic is exhausting when your spine feels filled with wet sand. Don't push yourself, Lilith. The volumes aren't going anywhere. They'll wait for you on the floor, patient as tombstones. #end
